", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Taking the Plunge", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will.</span><br/>You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action in the future before another action in the future. This is the past in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have started before that moment, but it will not have finished at that moment. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the Future Perfect tense like the Present Perfect tense, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Continuous and Future Perfect tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be going to/ will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I also <span class=\\\"strong\\\">won't be working</span> in the evening.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You girls <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have eaten</span> the best food.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I hope those shoes won't have hurt your feet by the end of the evening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He'll be here by then.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I know I will not be working Saturday brunch and I also won't be working in the evening.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So I won't be doing anything.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "After tonight, you girls will have eaten the best food, seen the best show around and have danced at the most popular nightclubs in town.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About Solving Problems", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">need + passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"italic\">need + verb + ing</span> to talk about things that need to be done.<br/> You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it itself.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"underline\">need + passive infinitive and need + verb + ing</span></span> to focus on the <span class=\"strong\">thing</span> that needs doing, not the person who is doing it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive<br/><span class=\"italic\">The restaurant <span class=\"strong\">needs to be run</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs doing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + need + verb + ing<br/><span class=\"italic\">The schedule<span class=\"strong\"> needs updating</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use need with a gerund (v-ing), it has a passive meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">causative verbs get/have</span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Have your spouse or housemates clean up after themselves. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this sentence <span class=\"italic\">you</span> ask or persuade your spouse to clean up after themselves.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the causative is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "have + object + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had</span> some extra <span class=\"strong\">servers come in</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "or ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + get + object + Infinitive ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got her to lend</span> me this necklace as well.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The restaurant needs to be run.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The staff needs organizing. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The schedule needs updating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Orders need to be made.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had some extra servers come in. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had an extra bartender come down tonight. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got my friend Sally to lend them to me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got her to lend me this necklace as well.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to look forward to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel happy and excited about something that is going to happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter told me that as soon as he arrives, we are going to an amazing place to eat. I'm looking forward to it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear to describe a special event!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "worth it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be good value for the cost", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope this is worth it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "have a good time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "enjoy oneself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are going to have a good time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extraordinary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely good or impressive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Extraordinary!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "intrigued ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be curious of unusual, new, or otherwise fascinating or compelling qualities ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am intrigued.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "popular", "type": "name"}, {"content": "regarded with favor and approval by many people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After tonight, you girls will have eaten the best food, seen the best show around and have danced at the most popular nightclubs in town.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "paint the town red", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go out and celebrate ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ladies, let's paint the town red.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you and your partner are travel agents creating a dream vacation package! ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide on a location of your dream vacation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then, you will create a poster that advertises the trip. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include at least 5 sentences that describe what people will do on your trip. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Also talk about what vacationers will be doing and what will be done for them to promote your trip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the phrase, by the time your trip ends \u2026 ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a 3 minute presentation to the rest of the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Vote on which pair has the best trip.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe a dream vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use Future tense, Future Perfect, and Future Progressive to describe my vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present vacation plans clearly and effectively. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback on others' vacation plans.  ", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}